---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageHero from '../../components/PageHero.astro';
import ContactSection from '../../components/ContactSection.astro';
import { site } from '../../data/site';

// Wording is carried over from the current live page. Changes from the live page:
//  - Meta description: "workers' comp lawyers" became singular (plan Section VIII, fix 6).
//  - Death benefits use the reviewed Workers' Comp page wording instead of the live page's
//    specific dollar figure and remarriage/age rules (those were never reviewed).
//  - "court" wording reworded: the Commission holds hearings and is not a court.
//  - "Settled, then got worse" FAQ answer reworded to agree with the reviewed settlement
//    wording (a full and final settlement closes the claim). Needs Bryn's review.
//  - Scheduled-injury FAQ is the live site's, unchanged; needs Bryn's review.
//  - Photo from the old page left out (source unknown).
const title = 'Virginia Construction Accident Attorney | Pathfinder Law';
const description =
  "Hurt in a construction accident? Speak to a Virginia workers' comp lawyer at Pathfinder Injury Law today. Call 804-505-0633 to get started.";
const h1 = 'Virginia Construction Accident Lawyer';
const path = '/virginia-construction-accident-lawyer/';

const toc = [
  { id: 'benefits', label: 'Your Virginia Construction Accident Benefits' },
  { id: 'denied', label: 'What to Do If Your Construction Accident Claim Is Denied' },
  { id: 'faq', label: 'Virginia Construction Accident FAQ' },
  { id: 'help', label: 'Get Help from a Construction Accident Lawyer in Virginia' },
];
---
<Base
  title={title}
  description={description}
  path={path}
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Workers’ Compensation Lawyer Serving Virginia', path: '/virginia-workers-comp-lawyer/' },
    { name: h1, path },
  ]}
  overlay
  author
>
  <PageHero
    title={h1}
    crumbs={[{ name: 'Workers’ Comp', href: '/virginia-workers-comp-lawyer/' }, { name: 'Construction Accidents' }]}
  />

  <div class="wrap page-body">
    <article class="prose">
      <p class="lead">
        Hurt in a Virginia construction accident? You may have grounds to get Workers’ Comp benefits,
        so don’t hesitate—get on the road to recovery with a Workers’ comp lawyer.
      </p>
      <p>
        Construction sites can be a dangerous place to work, but you know what to expect when you’re
        there. You may have been as careful as possible, too, until the accident happened. Now, you’re
        hurt, and to top it off, your family is suffering for it. You may have been the breadwinner of
        the household, and now, you may be unable to take care of yourself and those you love without
        help.
      </p>
      <p>
        At Pathfinder Law, we know how difficult your recovery from a construction accident can be.
        That’s why you may need help from a Virginia construction accident lawyer. We’ve got the tools
        you need to get the funds you need now, while you’re hurt and unable to work. You need help
        getting back on your feet and on the right path, and we’re here to guide you through it.
      </p>

      <h2 id="benefits">Your Virginia Construction Accident Benefits</h2>
      <p>
        Your Virginia construction accident can leave you with more than a serious injury. That injury
        impacts whether you’re able to work, your income, and your family. Because of this, you need a
        construction accident lawyer who can ensure you’re getting the Workers’ Comp benefits you need.
      </p>
      <p>
        It’s not easy to determine this without help from a lawyer. You just want to get back to work,
        or you want to focus on your recovery. Your construction accident lawyer in Virginia can focus
        on the details of your <a href="/virginia-workers-comp-lawyer/">Workers’ Comp claim</a> so you
        can focus on your health and family.
      </p>

      <h3>Medical Costs</h3>
      <p>
        After your Virginia construction accident, you may need immediate medical attention.
        Construction accidents can do a lot of damage, from head trauma to broken bones to severe
        burns. Getting treatment now helps you recover from those serious injuries, and it gives your
        claim a clearer timeline. Luckily, once your benefits are approved, your
        <a href="https://workcomp.virginia.gov/documents/injured-workers-benefits-guide" rel="noopener">medical expenses are covered by your Workers’ Comp</a>.
      </p>
      <p>
        You may be due funds for other losses, too. For example, you may need specialists, and those
        specialists may be a few cities over, meaning you have some traveling to do. Your lawyer can
        help you get compensated for all the costs that come with getting your health back.
      </p>

      <h3>Disability Benefits</h3>
      <p>
        You may not be able to work, but that doesn’t mean your bills will stop coming. You need
        disability benefits that replace a portion of your wages so you can support yourself and your
        family while you’re unable to work. In many cases, you’ll be offered two-thirds of your income
        before your Virginia construction accident, but your construction accident lawyer can help you
        determine this.
      </p>

      <h3>Death Benefits</h3>
      <p>
        You may not have been the one injured in a Virginia construction accident, but instead you lost
        a loved one in a fatal construction accident. You’re not just grieving—you’re dealing with the
        aftermath of losing their financial support.
      </p>
      <p>
        Your loved one’s Workers’ Compensation benefits can help you recover from your financial
        losses. Workers’ comp can provide death benefits to the family of a worker who loses their life
        because of a workplace injury. These benefits can pay for a limited amount of funeral expenses,
        medical bills incurred before the death, and lost wages for certain periods of time for certain
        survivors or dependents who meet statutory criteria.
      </p>

      <div class="pull">
        <p><strong>Learn how we can help you with your construction accident Workers’ Comp case.</strong></p>
        <p><a class="btn btn-primary" href="#contact">Get Help Now</a></p>
      </div>

      <h2 id="denied">What to Do If Your Virginia Construction Accident Claim Is Denied</h2>
      <p>
        When you’re hurt in a construction accident, it may seem pretty obvious to you that you’re due
        compensation for your injuries. In these cases, then, it may be a big shock to get a Workers’
        Comp letter in the mail stating you were denied.
      </p>
      <p>
        Don’t give up on your claim just because you were denied once. You can act now with a Workers’
        Comp lawyer to fight to get that denial overturned. Your lawyer’s got the tools to take your
        claim to a hearing before the Virginia Workers’ Compensation Commission. Your lawyer can help
        you prepare for your hearing and maximize your chances of getting your benefits.
      </p>
      <p><a href="/how-to-appeal-a-workers-comp-denial-in-virginia/">Workers’ Comp Denials</a></p>

      <h2 id="faq">Virginia Construction Accident FAQ</h2>
      <p>
        After a serious construction accident, it’s not always easy to get answers about your Workers’
        Comp benefits. As a Virginia construction worker, you may be eligible for help, but that may be
        easier said than done. Without legal experience, it’s easy to get confused and lost in the
        legal jargon and hearings.
      </p>
      <p>
        We can help guide you through this process. If you’re confused, below are some of our most
        commonly asked questions. We can answer these questions and more in a one-on-one consultation,
        too, so you know that we’re on your side before your hearing. Check out the questions below to
        learn more about the services we can offer.
      </p>
      <div class="faq">
        <details>
          <summary>Can I sue someone for my Virginia construction accident?</summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <p>
              If you’re a Virginia construction worker, your best option may be to request Workers’ Comp
              benefits. But that doesn’t mean you can’t sue in some cases. Let’s say your employer
              intentionally injured you or was doing something illegal. You may not be able to trust
              them with your Workers’ Comp benefits. If you’re unsure about your benefits, talk it over
              with your construction accident lawyer.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What is a scheduled injury in Virginia?</summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <p>
              Certain injuries only get a defined number of weeks for benefits. These injuries, called
              scheduled injuries, cover the loss of use of a body part, like an arm or toe. For
              example, if you lose use of your thumb, you may receive disability benefits
              <a href="https://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/title65.2/chapter5/section65.2-503/" rel="noopener">for sixty weeks based on this schedule</a>.
              Permanent partial disability benefits are only available for the body parts listed in
              <a href="https://law.lis.virginia.gov/vacode/title65.2/chapter5/section65.2-503/" rel="noopener">Virginia Code § 65.2-503</a>.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>What if I settle my Workers’ Comp claim, but then my construction injury gets worse?</summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <p>
              Your initial agreement may not cover all the losses you’ve suffered because of a Virginia
              construction accident. You may have thought your concussion would improve within a few
              weeks, for example, but a month has passed and you still have symptoms.
            </p>
            <p>
              Once 30 days pass from the deputy commissioner entering the settlement order, the case is
              done and cannot be revived. Your construction accident lawyer can review your agreement
              and tell you where you stand.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Do I need a construction accident lawyer?</summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <p>
              You may think you have an open-and-shut case, and you’re clearly eligible for Workers’
              Comp benefits. But what if something goes wrong? A mistake could lead to being denied your
              Virginia Workers’ Comp. You don’t have to take risks when you have a lawyer on your side.
              Your lawyer can guide you to the right answers and help you seek your benefits.
            </p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How long will it take to get my Workers’ Comp claim approved after an accident?</summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <p>
              After a construction accident, you need funds as soon as possible. Those bills won’t wait,
              but what if your Workers’ Comp claim takes a long time? With a construction accident
              lawyer in Virginia, you can get the help you need to speed up the process. Your lawyer can
              focus on getting your claim settled fast, without sacrificing the full funds you need.
            </p>
            <p><a href="/virginia-workers-comp-lawyer/how-long-do-virginia-workers-comp-settlements-take/">Learn More</a></p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>If I Get Injured at Work in Virginia, Do I Get Paid?</summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <p>
              After a serious work injury, working may be out of the question. When you’re injured at
              work in Virginia, you need to get paid, but you can’t get your usual paycheck. So how do
              you pay for your needs after an accident?
            </p>
            <p>
              Your lawyer at Pathfinder Injury Law has the tools you need to get paid after a work
              injury. We can guide you to the benefits you need when you’re struggling to overcome your
              work injuries.
            </p>
            <p><a href="/virginia-workers-comp-lawyer/if-i-get-injured-at-work-in-virginia-do-i-get-paid/">Learn More</a></p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>How do you Prepare for an IME in Virginia?</summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <p>
              After a work accident, you may be expected to take an independent medical exam, or IME.
              These appointments help the insurance company gauge your injuries and how seriously you
              suffered. But that means they may be trying to trip you up, tricking you into showing
              that you’re not really that injured.
            </p>
            <p>
              Because of this, you need to know how to prepare for an IME in Virginia. Luckily, our
              dedicated team at Pathfinder Injury Law has some tips to help you get ready and can
              represent you at every step of the Workers’ Comp process.
            </p>
            <p><a href="/virginia-workers-comp-lawyer/how-to-prepare-for-an-ime-in-virginia/">Learn More</a></p>
          </div>
        </details>
        <details>
          <summary>Does Virginia Workers’ Comp Pay for Lost Wages?</summary>
          <div class="answer">
            <p>
              After a serious work injury in Virginia, you may be directed to your Workers’ Comp
              benefits to recover from your injuries. You can’t cover your bills and needs without your
              wages, so it’s vital that you get coverage.
            </p>
            <p>
              But does Virginia Workers’ Comp pay for lost wages? If you’re worried about losing your
              wages, reach out to Pathfinder Injury Law. We can help you seek out the coverage you need
              from your Workers’ Comp provider.
            </p>
            <p><a href="/virginia-workers-comp-lawyer/does-virginia-workers-comp-pay-for-lost-wages/">Learn More</a></p>
          </div>
        </details>
      </div>

      <div class="pull" id="help">
        <h2>Get Help from a Construction Accident Lawyer in Virginia</h2>
        <p>
          A serious Virginia construction accident can impact your life for years to come. But you have
          options. When you are unsure where to turn, it’s easy to make a mistake and lose the benefits
          you need.
        </p>
        <p>
          That’s where a Virginia construction accident lawyer can help. At <a href="/">Pathfinder Law</a>,
          we’re here to guide you through your claim, starting with a free consultation about your
          construction accident. Take advantage of our consultations by calling
          <a href={site.phoneHref}>804-505-0633</a> or by completing our
          <a href="#contact">online contact form</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <aside class="side" aria-label="Page navigation and contact">
      <div class="side-card side-call">
        <h2>Free Consultation</h2>
        <a class="cta-phone" href={site.phoneHref}>{site.phoneDisplay}</a>
        <a class="btn btn-primary" href="#contact">Get Help Now</a>
      </div>
      <nav class="side-card" aria-label="On this page">
        <h2>On This Page</h2>
        <ul class="toc">
          {toc.map((t) => <li><a href={`#${t.id}`}>{t.label}</a></li>)}
        </ul>
      </nav>
    </aside>
  </div>

  <ContactSection />
</Base>
